      "failureSummary": "Implemented the scrypt password-hashing module for the TaskBoard backend. Added src/password.js (node:crypto only): hashPassword() draws a fresh per-user salt from crypto.randomBytes(16) and derives a 64-byte key via crypto.scryptSync with explicit frozen cost parameters (N=16384, r=8, p=1, maxmem=64MiB), returning only the persistable fields password_algo ('scrypt'), password_salt (hex) and password_hash (hex) - never the plaintext. Added isValidPasswordHash() (structural validation of untrusted stored records) and verifyPassword() (constant-time timingSafeEqual comparison) so the stored record can be revalidated by a later login slice. All functions treat arguments as untrusted: non-string, empty or malformed input yields a generic TypeError or false without echoing any value. Refactored src/register.js to consume the shared module and re-export PASSWORD_ALGO/hashPassword/verifyPassword, preserving the existing export surface and API contract. Remaining failure in the full suite is the 8 pre-existing README/docs tests in test/docs.test.js (AC-30 documentation slice), which is outside this task's scope; every register/auth/data-safety test is green.",
